WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.200
This is a digest-pinned nginx image, tested as built.

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:11.600
A static check reads what the image declares. SPEC-01 reports: Image runs as root user (configured user: '').

3
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:24.000
It runs as root. Would it still start if an operator dropped every capability?

4
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.000
Tier 3 starts the image again under one restriction at a time.

5
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:37.400
With a read-only root filesystem and a writable /tmp, the container exited with code 1.

6
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:42.000
The last log line is a mkdir error: Read-only file system.

7
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:49.000
Three suspects: the image, the restriction, the test setup.

8
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.400
A dead container alone does not say which.

9
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.400
The baseline runs first, with defensive flags only. It is still running at W.

10
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.000
Because it was running, the treatment is judged.

11
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.000
The restricted run exited. The result is FAIL.

12
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.800
It did not survive W although the baseline did. That is not a defect claim and not a root cause.

13
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.000
The alpine baseline exited with code 0 before W. There is no long-running process to observe.

14
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.600
The treatment is not judged. The result is UNVERIFIED with reason NOT_OBSERVABLE.

15
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.800
No verdict is better than a guess.

16
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.500
The haproxy baseline did not stay running. It exited with a non-zero code.

17
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.600
The result is UNVERIFIED with reason BASELINE_FAILED. The log says the configuration file is missing.

18
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:41.800
The console report groups the checks of one image by outcome.

19
00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.800
PASS, FAIL and UNVERIFIED are different outcomes.

20
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:55.600
Each FAIL lists its message and a next step. For Tier 3, the message says what the container did.

21
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.600
UNVERIFIED carries a reason from a closed set. Here SUP-02 has NO_TRUST_POLICY.

22
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.200
SUP-02 is a Tier 4 check. Tier 4 is an interface only and is not part of the evaluation.

23
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.800
An UNVERIFIED result is never counted as a pass.

24
00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:15.800
Attribution is done by the evaluation tool tools/attribute_exec, not by con-unit test in version 0.3.0.

25
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.600
The baseline runs and the treatment exits. Then each candidate path is made writable, one at a time.

26
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:29.800
Making /var/cache writable restores liveness at W. The union of all candidates does too.

27
00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:34.600
The recorded status is RESOLVED_SINGLE. It is a lead for a recipe, not a proof.

28
00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.200
The same steps for the capability restriction. Dropping all capabilities makes the run exit.

29
00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:45.800
No single capability restores the run, but all candidates together do.

30
00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:52.000
Then capabilities are removed from the set one at a time, and the run is checked after each removal.

31
00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.400
The minimal set that restores liveness at W: CAP_CHOWN, CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE.

32
00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:59.600
It is a lead for a recipe, not a proof.

33
00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:04.000
ConUnit runs where tests run. One command tests an image.

34
00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.000
This live run used rootless Podman 5.8.1, arm64, not the evaluation setup.

35
00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.000
The exit code is 1 when a result is FAIL or UNVERIFIED.

36
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:17.600
In the JUnit file, an UNVERIFIED result is a skipped testcase and a FAIL is a failure.

37
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:24.600
Go tests can call the same checks. This example from the repository compiles as recorded.

38
00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:29.350
Running at W is a liveness proxy, not proof that a service works.

39
00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:32.850
Attribution is done by the evaluation tool tools/attribute_exec, not by con-unit test.

40
00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:36.350
Tiers 1 and 2 overlap with linters like Dockle and the Anchore CIS pack.

41
00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.850
Tier 4 is an interface only and is not part of the evaluation.

42
00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.350
The profile is informed by CIS topics. It is not a CIS compliance assessment.

43
00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.850
Tier 3 starts the image with its own entrypoint. Use a disposable host.

44
00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:50.350
A baseline that fails or exits early gives UNVERIFIED, not a guess.

45
00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:52.600
Evaluated so far on rootful Podman 4.9.3, linux/amd64.

46
00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.750
Research prototype. Evaluation results are not repeated here.

47
00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:01.000
The quick start from the README: run the unit tests, build the binary, test one image.

48
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:07.200
ConUnit 0.3.0 is a research prototype under the MIT license.

49
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:14.000
The repository link will be added after publication.
